                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1428-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>SE Electronics X1R</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Bidirectional Ribbon Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The X1R is a passive ribbon microphone with a 2-micron aluminum ribbon. </p><p>According to sE Electronics, the mic&#8217;s cost is kept low by repurposing the body and chassis of the X1 condenser.</p><p>The X1R uses a mechanical acoustic filter in front of the ribbon (both front and back sides) to produce a high-frequency lift not commonly found in older ribbon designs. This technology is borrowed from the VR1/VR2 &#8220;Voodoo&#8221; ribbon line. </p><p>The mic has a figure-8 polar pattern, with a symmetrical response. (Although two graphs are published in the cutsheet PDF, these do not represent front and back response &#8212; rather, the lower graph is a sensitivity graph.)<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/SE-Electronics/X1R">SE Electronics X1R</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2011.</p>
